body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When `provisionalSafeContextAllowed` is `false`, we should explicitly verify that `assertion?.downgraded_context_eligible` is not `true` (or is falsy). This ensures that the schema validator is fully aligned with the gate validator (`validateAcceptedOnlySemanticAnswerFactGate`), which asserts `provisional_safe_downgrade_requires_context_posture` under the same conditions.

Adding this check prevents any tampered or malformed payloads with unauthorized downgrade eligibility from passing the schema validation phase. Additionally, please ensure that unit tests for this validator are updated to cover this new check and explicitly test the malformed-input guard paths.

```suggestion
    if (provisionalSafeContextAllowed && assertion?.downgraded_context_eligible !== true) {
      errors.push(errorWithFixture(fixtureId, 'provisional_safe_missing_downgrade_context'));
    }
    if (!provisionalSafeContextAllowed && assertion?.downgraded_context_eligible === true) {
      errors.push(errorWithFixture(fixtureId, 'provisional_safe_downgrade_requires_context_posture'));
    }
```

